  "behavior": {
    "viewport": "Cached strict presentation is used for active raw echo, character deletion and restoration. Known stdout geometry reserves the final column and caps the row at 256 columns. Tail selection uses cached token offsets/widths; no raw bytes or full-draft copy on repaint. CR and spaces rewrite the row without ANSI capabilities.",
    "fallback": "Widths unknown or below ten columns use labelled snapshots bounded to 80 columns; snapshots may wrap naturally. No destructive cursor movement is guessed. Complete request guidance remains outside compact editable rows.",
    "ownership": "Native output supplies its channel and resolved stat identity. Prompt geometry follows stdout, ignores unrelated redirected stderr, and abandons old geometry on replacement/resize. One fixed old-destination boundary can separate diagnostics there without repainting the new row. Controller revisions invalidate presentation on input/request mutations; raw submission and its line boundary use one operation.",
    "admission": "Only exactly empty ordinary messages are ignored before queueing. Whitespace-only ordinary messages and empty request answers retain their meanings. Submission classification supplies a discard reason only on rejection; external answer rejection explicitly reports expiry.",
    "diagnostics": "Main-thread configured-sink and restoration fallbacks use the invocation writer. Interactive worker cleanup failures set allocation-free fixed warning bits on Interaction, coalesced by kind and drained only by the main thread, including after quiescence. No ambient global cancellation context or new lock.",
    "delivery": "Discard instruction success is independent of prompt success. Keyboard row updates remain best effort and do not latch a new display error; checked prompt/reply failures remain sticky. Raw data, storage/journal authority and diagnostic replay order are unchanged.",
    "input_bytes": 65536,
    "row_columns": 256,
    "snapshot_columns": 80,
    "row_buffers_bytes": 1536,
    "line_owner_size_baseline_arm64": 200,
